3.8-Max 按积分计费，官方推出了 分时段折扣 ：\\n常规时段 （每日 08:00–22:00，UTC+8）：原价 1x；\\n错峰时段 （每日 22:00–次日 08:00，UTC+8）： 5 折（0.5x） ，含周末与节假日。\\n无需报名、无需领取 ，把 Qoder 更新到最新版、切换 Qwen3.8-Max，错峰时段发起请求即自动享受 5 折。\\n两个你可能关心的问题：\\n折扣影响的是 积分计价 ，模型质量、推理能力、上下文长度都不变；\\n错峰时段消耗的积分 计入月度套餐额度 ，属于折扣计费而非额外赠送；\\n折扣结束时间暂未确定，官方会提前通知，建议尽早用起来。\\n\\n五、三步上手，马上开领\\n更新客户端 ：把 Qoder Desktop / JetBrains 插件 / Qoder CLI / QoderWake 任一更新到最新版本；\\n登录领取 ：登录账号，在端内「用量」面板点击领取（下单赠送额度也需手动领取）；\\n切换模型 ：在模型档位选择器中切换到 Qwen3.8-Max ，开始使用。\\n\\n写在最后\\n这波福利的核心时间点再帮你理一遍：\\n活动截止 ：2026 年 9 月 3 日 23:59（UTC+8）——领取免费次数、下单叠加、完成邀请都在这之前；\\n免费次数到期 ：2026 年 9 月 30 日 23:59（UTC+8）——领了尽快用，过期作废；\\n领取无门槛限制端 ：Desktop / JetBrains 插件 / CLI / QoderWake 任一客户端都行。\\n千问 3.8-Max 本身已经够强，叠加这波周年福利，正是低成本体验旗舰模型的好时机。如果你觉得对同事朋友也有用，别忘把下面这条专属链接分享给他们，邀请返 400 积分，越邀越划算：\\nhttps://qoder.com.cn/referral?referral_code=sa2ErPynesYONip60A8CzBL4yEtQ0WIu", "publish_time": "2026年08月10日", "auth_level": "", "authority_weight": 0.0}, "182": {"url": "https://openclawpulse.com/best-free-models-openclaw/", "title": "Best Free Models for OpenClaw in 2026 — Run Your AI Agent for $0", "page_content": "运行OpenClaw完全免费，无需花费一分钱。具体操作方法如下。\\n上述段落英文原文为：You don’t need to spend a penny to run OpenClaw. Here’s exactly how.\\n许多人误以为运行OpenClaw（原ClawdBot，后短暂使用MoltBot）需要付费API订阅，其实不然。通过OpenRouter的免费套餐、服务商免费计划，以及基于OAuth的访问方式，你完全可以运行一个功能完整的OpenClaw代理——无论是Telegram、Discord、WhatsApp，还是你选择的任何其他平台——而无需花费任何费用。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Most people assume running OpenClaw (formerly ClawdBot, briefly MoltBot) requires a paid API subscription. It doesn’t. Between OpenRouter’s free tier, provider free plans, and OAuth-based access, you can run a fully functional OpenClaw agent — across Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, or whatever your platform of choice is — without spending anything.\\n不过需要注意的是：免费模型确实存在一些权衡。本指南将详细介绍目前实际可用的选项、如何配置每个选项，以及免费套餐在哪些情况下已经不够用了。\\n上述段落英文原文为：The catch? Free models have tradeoffs. This guide covers what’s actually available right now, how to set each option up, and where the free tier stops being good enough.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">OpenClaw的免费模型现状</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">The Free Model Landscape for OpenClaw</quark-heading>\\n截至2026年2月，有四种实用的免费运行OpenClaw的方式：\\n上述段落英文原文为：As of February 2026, there are four practical routes to running OpenClaw for free:\\nKimi K2.5 — OpenRouter上免费（也可通过Moonshot直接使用）\\n上述段落英文原文为：Kimi K2.5 — free on OpenRouter (and via Moonshot directly)\\nPony Alpha — OpenRouter上免费\\n上述段落英文原文为：Pony Alpha — free on OpenRouter\\nMinimax — 7天免费试用，配额相当慷慨\\n上述段落英文原文为：Minimax — 7-day free trial with generous limits\\nChatGPT Codex — 通过OpenAI OAuth免费使用（Codex需要OpenAI订阅，但Plus/Pro用户免费）\\n上述段落英文原文为：ChatGPT Codex — free via OpenAI OAuth (requires OpenAI subscription for Codex, but free for Plus/Pro users)\\n当然还有常年可用的选项：Google Gemini的免费套餐、Groq的免费API，以及OpenRouter免费模型路由器（从所有可用的免费模型中随机选择）。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Plus the perennial options: Google Gemini’s free tier , Groq’s free API , and the OpenRouter free model router that randomly selects from all available free models.\\n我们来逐一详细说明。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Let’s break each one down.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">1. Kimi K2.5 — 当前免费模型之王</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">1. Kimi K2.5 — The Current King of Free</quark-heading>\\nMoonshot AI的Kimi K2.5目前是OpenRouter上OpenClaw用户使用最频繁的模型，这不是炒作——这是真实使用数据。开发者选择它是因为它在零成本的情况下提供了接近Claude Sonnet 4.5的推理质量。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Kimi K2.5 from Moonshot AI is currently the #1 most-used model on OpenRouter for OpenClaw users. That’s not hype — it’s usage data. Developers chose it because it delivers reasoning quality close to Claude Sonnet 4.5 at zero cost.\\n你能获得什么：完整的工具调用支持、128K上下文窗口、强大的编程和推理能力。Moonshot已经宣布在其平台上永久免费开放访问。\\n上述段落英文原文为：What you get: Full tool-calling support, 128K context window, strong coding and reasoning. Moonshot has announced permanent free access on their platform.\\n限制条件：在OpenRouter免费套餐下有速率限制（大约每分钟20次请求，每日重置）。通过Moonshot自己的API，配额更宽松但需要单独注册账户。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Limits: Rate-limited on OpenRouter’s free tier (roughly 20 requests/minute, resets daily). Via Moonshot’s own API, limits are more generous but require a separate account.\\n配置方法（OpenRouter）：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Setup (OpenRouter):\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n或者在\\n上述段落英文原文为：Or in\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenclaw.json\\n上述段落英文原文为：openclaw.json\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n中配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：:\\n<quark-code>{\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>{\\n\"agents\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"agents\": {\\n\"defaults\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"defaults\": {\\n\"model\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"model\": {\\n\"primary\": \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"primary\": \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>}</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>}</quark-code>\\n最佳用途：通用代理工作、编程任务、研究、内容起草。这是入门的首选。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Best for: General-purpose agent work, coding tasks, research, content drafting. This is the one to start with.\\n质量：★★★★☆ —— 与中端付费模型真正竞争。在非常复杂的多步推理任务上偶尔会有些不足。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★★★☆ — Genuinely competitive with mid-tier paid models. Occasional weaknesses on very complex multi-step reasoning.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">2. Pony Alpha — Surprisingly Capable</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">2. Pony Alpha — Surprisingly Capable</quark-heading>\\nPony Alpha 是 OpenRouter 上一个不太知名的免费模型。作为免费选项，它表现超出了预期，具备不错的工具调用支持和合理的上下文处理能力。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Pony Alpha is a lesser-known free model available on OpenRouter. It punches above its weight for a free option, with decent tool-calling support and reasonable context handling.\\n限制：OpenRouter 的免费套餐，有标准的速率限制。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Limits: Free tier on OpenRouter with standard rate limits.\\n配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Setup:\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/pony-alpha\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/pony-alpha\"\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n最佳用途：较轻量的任务 —— 快速查询、简单自动化、心跳任务。在分层设置中适合作为备用模型使用。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Best for: Lighter tasks — quick lookups, simple automations, heartbeat duties. Works well as a fallback model in a tiered setup.\\n质量：★★★☆☆ —— 适合简单任务。在复杂推理链或长对话中开始出现困难。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★★☆☆ — Good for simple tasks. Starts to struggle with complex reasoning chains or long multi-turn conversations.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">3. Minimax — Premium Feel, Free Trial</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">3. Minimax — Premium Feel, Free Trial</quark-heading>\\nMinimax 提供 7 天免费试用，可使用其旗舰模型。社区共识认为它更适合写作和对话任务，而不是编程 —— 正如 OpenClaw 文档中所说的\"氛围模型\"。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Minimax offers a 7-day free trial with access to their flagship model. The community consensus is that it’s better for writing and conversational tasks than for coding — the “vibes” model, as the OpenClaw docs put it.\\n限制：7 天试用期。试用结束后，您需要付费或切换。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Limits: 7-day trial period. After that, you’ll need to pay or switch.\\n配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Setup:\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/minimax/minimax-01\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/minimax/minimax-01\"\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n最佳用途：内容创作、对话代理、创意任务。如果您主要使用 OpenClaw 进行写作，建议先尝试 Minimax。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Best for: Content creation, conversational agents, creative tasks. If you’re using OpenClaw primarily for writing, try Minimax first.\\n质量：★★★★☆ —— 写作质量优秀。与 Kimi K2.5 相比，在结构化工具使用和代码生成方面稍弱。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★★★☆ — Excellent writing quality. Weaker on structured tool use and code generation compared to Kimi K2.5.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">4. ChatGPT Codex via OAuth</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">4. ChatGPT Codex via OAuth</quark-heading>\\n如果您已经拥有 OpenAI Plus 或 Pro 订阅，可以通过 OAuth 将 OpenClaw 连接到 ChatGPT 的 Codex 模型 —— 不需要单独的 API 密钥。从技术上讲，如果您正在为 ChatGPT 付费，这不算真正免费，但如果您已经是订阅用户，额外成本为零。\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you already have an OpenAI Plus or Pro subscription, you can connect OpenClaw to ChatGPT’s Codex model via OAuth — no separate API key needed. Technically this isn’t “free” if you’re paying for ChatGPT, but if you’re already a subscriber, it costs nothing extra.\\n配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Setup:\\n<quark-code>openclaw onboard\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw onboard\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 在浏览器中完成OAuth流程</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code># Follow the OAuth flow in your browser</quark-code>\\n最佳用途：已经为ChatGPT付费的用户，希望使用OpenClaw而无需额外的API费用。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Best for: Users who already pay for ChatGPT and want to use OpenClaw without additional API costs.\\n质量：★★★★☆ —— 功能全面的通用模型，工具调用表现优秀。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★★★☆ — Solid general-purpose model with good tool calling.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">5. 附加推荐：Google Gemini免费版</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">5. Bonus: Google Gemini Free Tier</quark-heading>\\n谷歌Gemini API经常被忽视，但其免费额度在业内非常慷慨：Gemini Flash版本每天1,500次请求，每分钟100万tokens。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Often overlooked, Google’s Gemini API has one of the most generous free tiers in the industry: 1,500 requests/day and 1 million tokens/minute on Gemini Flash.\\n配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Setup:\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"\\n# 通过openclaw onboard设置Gemini API密钥，或：\\n上述段落英文原文为：# Set your Gemini API key via openclaw onboard or:\\nopenclaw config set models.providers.google.apiKey \"YOUR_KEY\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：openclaw config set models.providers.google.apiKey \"YOUR_KEY\"\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n最佳用途：高频率使用场景。如果你的OpenRouter免费模型已达到调用限制，Gemini Flash的免费额度可以说是极其慷慨。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Best for: High-volume usage. If you’re hitting rate limits on OpenRouter free models, Gemini Flash’s free tier is absurdly generous.\\n质量：★★★★☆ —— 响应迅速，功能强大，适合大多数日常任务。但在复杂推理任务上不如前沿模型表现突出。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★★★☆ — Fast, capable, excellent for most daily tasks. Not as strong as frontier models on complex reasoning.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">6. OpenRouter免费模型路由器</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">6. OpenRouter Free Model Router</quark-heading>\\n不想手动选择？OpenRouter提供\\n上述段落英文原文为：Don’t want to pick? OpenRouter offers\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n——这是一个元模型，会随机将你的请求路由到当前可用的任意免费模型。\\n上述段落英文原文为：— a meta-model that randomly routes your requests to whichever free models are currently available.\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/openrouter/free\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/openrouter/free\"\\nopenclaw config unset agents.defaults.models\\n上述段落英文原文为：openclaw config unset agents.defaults.models\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n质量：★★½☆☆ —— 设计上存在不一致性。适合测试使用，但由于无法预测响应模型，不适合生产环境。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Quality: ★★½☆☆ — Inconsistent by design. Fine for testing, not ideal for production use since you can’t predict which model will respond.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">对比表格</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Comparison Table</quark-heading>\\n<quark-table><table><thead><tr><th>模型</th><th>提供商</th><th>免费版限制</th><th>质量</th><th>速度</th><th>最佳用途</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Kimi K2.5</td><td>OpenRouter / Moonshot</td><td>约每分钟20次请求，每日重置</td><td>★★★★</td><td>快速</td><td>通用代理工作、编程</td></tr><tr><td>Pony Alpha</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>标准免费限制</td><td>★★★</td><td>快速</td><td>简单任务、备用选择</td></tr><tr><td>Minimax</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>7天试用</td><td>★★★★</td><td>中等</td><td>写作、创意任务</td></tr><tr><td>Codex (OAuth)</td><td>OpenAI</td><td>与ChatGPT订阅绑定</td><td>★★★★</td><td>中等</td><td>现有ChatGPT用户</td></tr><tr><td>Gemini Flash</td><td>Google</td><td>每日1,500次请求，每分钟1M个token</td><td>★★★★</td><td>极快</td><td>高频率日常使用</td></tr><tr><td>Groq (Llama 3.1 70B)</td><td>Groq</td><td>每日14,400次请求</td><td>★★★½</td><td>最快</td><td>对速度要求极高的任务</td></tr><tr><td>openrouter/free</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>因情况而异</td><td>★★½</td><td>因情况而异</td><td>实验性使用</td></tr></tbody></table></quark-table>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-table><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Provider</th><th>Free Tier Limits</th><th>Quality</th><th>Speed</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Kimi K2.5</td><td>OpenRouter / Moonshot</td><td>~20 req/min, daily reset</td><td>★★★★</td><td>Fast</td><td>General agent work, coding</td></tr><tr><td>Pony Alpha</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>Standard free limits</td><td>★★★</td><td>Fast</td><td>Simple tasks, fallback</td></tr><tr><td>Minimax</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>7-day trial</td><td>★★★★</td><td>Medium</td><td>Writing, creative tasks</td></tr><tr><td>Codex (OAuth)</td><td>OpenAI</td><td>Tied to ChatGPT sub</td><td>★★★★</td><td>Medium</td><td>Existing ChatGPT users</td></tr><tr><td>Gemini Flash</td><td>Google</td><td>1,500 req/day, 1M tok/min</td><td>★★★★</td><td>Very fast</td><td>High-volume daily use</td></tr><tr><td>Groq (Llama 3.1 70B)</td><td>Groq</td><td>14,400 req/day</td><td>★★★½</td><td>Fastest</td><td>Speed-critical tasks</td></tr><tr><td>openrouter/free</td><td>OpenRouter</td><td>Varies</td><td>★★½</td><td>Varies</td><td>Experimentation</td></tr></tbody></table></quark-table>\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">诚实的权衡：免费版能做什么和不能做什么</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">The Honest Tradeoff: What Free Can and Can’t Do</quark-heading>\\n免费模型擅长处理：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Free models handle well:\\n心跳检测和后台监控\\n上述段落英文原文为：Heartbeat checks and background monitoring\\n简单查询（日历、天气、快速搜索）\\n上述段落英文原文为：Simple lookups (calendar, weather, quick searches)\\n消息草稿和基础内容生成\\n上述段落英文原文为：Drafting messages and basic content\\n直接的编程任务（单文件编辑、脚本）\\n上述段落英文原文为：Straightforward coding tasks (single-file edits, scripts)\\n子代理协调任务\\n上述段落英文原文为：Sub-agent coordination tasks\\n作为基础个人助理运行ClawdBot或MoltBot\\n上述段落英文原文为：Running ClawdBot or MoltBot as a basic personal assistant\\n您可能需要付费模型的情况：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Where you’ll want a paid model:\\n复杂的多文件重构\\n上述段落英文原文为：Complex multi-file refactoring\\n需要深度推理的架构决策\\n上述段落英文原文为：Architectural decisions requiring deep reasoning\\n长篇幅、复杂且上下文依赖度高的多轮对话\\n上述段落英文原文为：Long, nuanced multi-turn conversations with high context dependence\\n需要一致、可预测输出质量的任务\\n上述段落英文原文为：Tasks requiring consistent, predictable output quality\\n对随机模型故障不可接受的关键生产流程\\n上述段落英文原文为：Production-critical workflows where random model failures aren’t acceptable\\n明智的做法是什么？使用分层设置。将Kimi K2.5或Gemini Flash作为主要模型，将Opus或GPT-5.2作为需要前沿级推理时的备用选择：\\n上述段落英文原文为：The smart move? Use a tiered setup. Put Kimi K2.5 or Gemini Flash as your primary, and save Opus or GPT-5.2 as a fallback for when you need frontier-level reasoning:\\n<quark-code>{\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>{\\n\"agents\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"agents\": {\\n\"defaults\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"defaults\": {\\n\"model\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"model\": {\\n\"primary\": \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\",\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"primary\": \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\",\\n\"fallbacks\": [\"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"]\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"fallbacks\": [\"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"]\\n},\\n上述段落英文原文为：},\\n\"heartbeat\": {\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"heartbeat\": {\\n\"model\": \"google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：\"model\": \"google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite\"\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n}\\n上述段落英文原文为：}\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>}</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>}</quark-code>\\n这为你提供了一个完全免费的OpenClaw配置，拥有快速强大的主模型和慷慨的免费层级备用方案。\\n上述段落英文原文为：This gives you a completely free OpenClaw setup with a fast, capable primary model and a generous-free-tier fallback.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">免费版 vs. 经济版：每月2美元值得吗？</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Free vs. Cheap: Is $2/Month Worth It?</quark-heading>\\n如果你愿意花费哪怕少量费用，你的选择就会大幅增加。以下是几美元能为你带来的收益：\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you’re willing to spend even a small amount, your options expand dramatically. Here’s what a few dollars gets you:\\n<quark-table><table><thead><tr><th>预算</th><th>配置</th><th>变化</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0美元/月</td><td>Kimi K2.5 + Gemini Flash 免费层级</td><td>完全可用，但有速率限制</td></tr><tr><td>1-2美元/月</td><td>DeepSeek V3.2（0.53美元/百万tokens）为主模型</td><td>无速率限制，质量稳定</td></tr><tr><td>3-5美元/月</td><td>DeepSeek R1用于推理 + Flash用于简单任务</td><td>以预算价格接近前沿的推理能力</td></tr><tr><td>10-20美元/月</td><td>Claude Sonnet 4.5或GPT-5为主模型</td><td>前沿质量，无任何妥协</td></tr></tbody></table></quark-table>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-table><table><thead><tr><th>Budget</th><th>Setup</th><th>What Changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>$0/mo</td><td>Kimi K2.5 + Gemini Flash free tiers</td><td>Fully functional, rate-limited</td></tr><tr><td>$1-2/mo</td><td>DeepSeek V3.2 ($0.53/M tokens) as primary</td><td>No rate limits, consistent quality</td></tr><tr><td>$3-5/mo</td><td>DeepSeek R1 for reasoning + Flash for simple tasks</td><td>Near-frontier reasoning at budget price</td></tr><tr><td>$10-20/mo</td><td>Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5 as primary</td><td>Frontier quality, no compromises</td></tr></tbody></table></quark-table>\\n对于大多数执行个人助理任务的MoltBot和ClawdBot用户来说，免费层级已经足够用了。如果你使用OpenClaw进行专业开发工作，即使在DeepSeek上每月花费2美元也能移除所有有意义的限制。\\n上述段落英文原文为：For most MoltBot and ClawdBot users doing personal assistant tasks, the free tier is genuinely enough. If you’re using OpenClaw for professional development work, even $2/month on DeepSeek removes every meaningful limitation.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">5分钟快速上手</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Getting Started in 5 Minutes</quark-heading>\\n如果你还没有安装OpenClaw：请参考 docs.openclaw.ai\\n上述段落英文原文为：Install OpenClaw if you haven’t: follow docs.openclaw.ai\\n在 openrouter.ai 获取OpenRouter API密钥（免费，无需信用卡）\\n上述段落英文原文为：Get an OpenRouter API key at openrouter.ai (free, no credit card)\\n运行配置：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Run the setup:\\n<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw config set agents.defaults.model.primary \"openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\"\\nopenclaw config set models.providers.openrouter.apiKey \"YOUR_OPENROUTER_KEY\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：openclaw config set models.providers.openrouter.apiKey \"YOUR_OPENROUTER_KEY\"\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw gateway restart</quark-code>\\n扫描可用的免费模型：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Scan available free models:\\n<quark-code>openclaw models scan</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>openclaw models scan</quark-code>\\n开始聊天。随时在对话中输入\\n上述段落英文原文为：Start chatting. Switch models anytime with\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n/model\\n上述段落英文原文为：/model\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n来切换模型。\\n上述段落英文原文为：in your conversation.\\n就完成了。零美元成本。一个完全可用的AI代理在你的机器上运行，连接到你选择的消息平台。\\n上述段落英文原文为：That’s it. Zero dollars. A fully functional AI agent running on your machine, connected to your messaging platform of choice.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">总结</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Bottom Line</quark-heading>\\nOpenClaw免费API生态系统比以往任何时候都更好了。Kimi K2.5单独就让免费层级对严肃的日常使用变得可行——它现在是OpenRouter上使用最频繁的模型，是有原因的。搭配Gemini Flash作为备用方案，你就拥有了一个零成本配置，能够处理大多数人90%的需求。\\n上述段落英文原文为：The openclaw free api ecosystem is better than it’s ever been. Kimi K2.5 alone makes the free tier viable for serious daily use — there’s a reason it’s the most-used model on OpenRouter right now. Pair it with Gemini Flash as a fallback and you’ve got a setup that costs nothing and handles 90% of what most people need.\\n剩下的10%？那是\\n上述段落英文原文为：The remaining 10%? That’s what\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n/model opus\\n上述段落英文原文为：/model opus\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n用于。但你可能会惊讶于自己有多少时候需要用到它。\\n上述段落英文原文为：is for. But you might be surprised how rarely you need it.\\n最后更新：2026年2月\\n上述段落英文原文为：Last updated: February 2026\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">继续阅读</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Keep Reading</quark-heading>\\n我以不到5美元/月的价格使用OpenClaw。具体做法如下。\\n上述段落英文原文为：I Run OpenClaw for Under $5/Month. Here’s Exactly How.\\nOpenClaw的成本是多少？2026年的实际费用明细\\n上述段落英文原文为：How Much Does OpenClaw Cost? A Real-World Breakdown for 2026\\n2026年OpenClaw的替代方案：哪些真正有效（以及何时使用）\\n上述段落英文原文为：OpenClaw Alternatives in 2026: What Actually Works (And When to Use Them)\\nAI代理的个人应用：今天真正能做到的有哪些\\n上述段落英文原文为：AI Agent for Personal Use: What’s Actually Possible Today", "publish_time": "2026年03月20日", "auth_level": "", "authority_weight": 0.0}, "183": {"url": "https://www.marketingscoop.com/developer/openrouter-free-model-explained-what-it-is-and-how-to-evaluate-it-before-your-team-depends-on-it/", "title": "OpenRouter Free Model Explained: What It Is and How to Evaluate It Before Your Team Depends on It", "page_content": "OpenRouter免费模型实用2026指南：详解\"openrouter/free\"和\":free\"的含义、当前限制、风险，以及团队可用的评估清单。\\n上述段落英文原文为：A practical 2026 guide to OpenRouter free models: what \"openrouter/free\" and \":free\" mean, current limits, risks, and a team-ready evaluation checklist.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">OpenRouter免费模型含义存在两种理解</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">OpenRouter Free Model Means Two Different Things</quark-heading>\\n人们搜索\"openrouter免费模型\"时，往往将其视为单一产品。但实际上，这通常指代两种不同的路由行为，这种差异直接决定了你的应用是否稳定或表现意外。\\n上述段落英文原文为：People search for \"openrouter free model\" as if it is one product. In practice, it usually means one of two routing behaviors, and this difference decides whether your app is stable or surprising. Networking\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">含义1：<quark-code>openrouter/free</quark-code>（免费路由）</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Meaning 1: <quark-code> openrouter/free </quark-code>(the free router)</quark-heading>\\n<quark-code>openrouter/free</quark-code>是一个路由模型ID。你发送一个请求，OpenRouter会从当前的免费模型池中选择一个免费模型。根据OpenRouter文档说明，该路由器会首先根据所需能力进行筛选，比如工具使用、图像输入或结构化输出，然后从兼容的免费选项中进行选择。\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code> openrouter/free </quark-code> is a router model ID. You send one request, and OpenRouter picks a free model from its current free pool. According to OpenRouter docs, this router filters by required capabilities first, like tool use, image input, or structured output, then chooses from compatible free options.\\n对于小项目来说，这种体验很神奇：零成本、无需模型选择、快速启动。但它也意味着你的后端模型可能在不同请求间发生变化，因为模型池和可用性会随时间变化。\\n上述段落英文原文为：For a small project, this feels magical: no cost, no model shopping, quick start. But it also means your backend model can change between requests, because the pool and availability change over time.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">含义2：<quark-code>:free</quark-code>（特定模型的免费版本）</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Meaning 2: <quark-code> :free </quark-code>(the free variant on a specific model)</quark-heading>\\n如果你请求类似\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you request something like\\n<quark-code>meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct:free</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code> meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct:free </quark-code>\\n的内容，你实际上是锁定了一个特定模型家族的免费层级。这比\\n上述段落英文原文为：, you are pinning a specific model family with a free tier. This is more predictable than\\n<quark-code>openrouter/free</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code> openrouter/free </quark-code>\\n更具可预测性，但仍与付费行为不完全相同。OpenRouter明确指出免费版本可能具有不同的可用性和限制。\\n上述段落英文原文为：, but still not identical to paid behavior. OpenRouter explicitly notes free variants can have different availability and limits.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">为什么这种区分很重要</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Why this distinction matters</quark-heading>\\n如果你在测试想法，\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you are testing ideas,\\n<quark-code>openrouter/free</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code> openrouter/free </quark-code>\\n通常没有问题。但如果你要发布功能，而输出风格和行为一致性很重要，那么在特定模型上使用\\n上述段落英文原文为：is usually fine. If you are shipping features where output style and behavior consistency matter,\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n:free\\n上述段落英文原文为：:free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n进行评估会更安全。如果你需要生产环境的可靠性，通常会转向付费端点，把免费模式主要用作非关键路径。\\n上述段落英文原文为：on a specific model is safer for evaluation. If you need production reliability, you normally move to paid endpoints and use free mostly as a non-critical lane.\\n了解更多\\n上述段落英文原文为：Discover more\\n路由器\\n上述段落英文原文为：router\\n路由器\\n上述段落英文原文为：Routers\\n编程\\n上述段落英文原文为：Programming\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">谁应该关注</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Who should care</quark-heading>\\n独立开发者：选择\\n上述段落英文原文为：Solo builders: choose\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n快速探索。\\n上述段落英文原文为：to explore quickly.\\n初创团队：在基准测试提示词和用户体验时使用\\n上述段落英文原文为：Startup teams: use\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n:free\\n上述段落英文原文为：:free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n。\\n上述段落英文原文为：while benchmarking prompts and UX.\\n产品经理和运维负责人：将\"免费\"视为评估输入，而不是可靠性承诺。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Product and ops leads: treat \"free\" as an evaluation input, not a reliability contract.\\n关键要点很简单：OpenRouter上的免费模式并不是一个简单的开关。它是一个路由策略决策。\\n上述段落英文原文为：The key takeaway is simple: free on OpenRouter is not one switch. It is a routing strategy decision.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">为什么这个术语在2026年比2024年更重要</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Why This Term Matters More in 2026 Than It Did in 2024</quark-heading>\\n这个话题已经从一个爱好问题变成了架构问题。原因不是炒作。原因在于免费模型路由已经成为真实开发者工作流程的重要组成部分，而模型目录和供应商格局变得更加动态。\\n上述段落英文原文为：This topic changed from a hobby question to an architecture question. The reason is not hype. The reason is that free model routing became a serious part of real developer workflows, while the model catalog and provider landscape became more dynamic.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">截至2026年3月30日的最新情况</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Fresh context as of March 30, 2026</quark-heading>\\n在OpenRouter上，专门的\\n上述段落英文原文为：On OpenRouter, the dedicated\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n路由器页面显示的发布时间为2026年2月1日。这一点很重要，因为现在团队拥有了首屈一指的免费路由器抽象功能，而不仅仅是临时的免费端点。\\n上述段落英文原文为：router page shows a release date of February 1, 2026. That matters because teams now have a first-class free router abstraction, not just ad hoc free endpoints.\\n网络设备\\n上述段落英文原文为：Networking Equipment\\n与此同时，OpenRouter的免费模型集合会根据当前的使用情况更新排名，组合可能会经常变化。用大白话说就是：你今天调用的免费模型可能不是下周在相同顶层路由下调用的模型。\\n上述段落英文原文为：At the same time, OpenRouter’s free model collection is updated with current usage-driven rankings, and the mix can change frequently. In plain language: the free model you hit today may not be the one you hit next week under the same top-level route.\\n了解更多\\n上述段落英文原文为：Discover more\\n网络\\n上述段落英文原文为：Networking\\n业务流程\\n上述段落英文原文为：Business Process\\n社会科学\\n上述段落英文原文为：Social Sciences\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">突破性转变</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">The breakout shift</quark-heading>\\n2024年，许多团队将\"免费模型\"当作玩具或演示功能来使用。到了2025年和2026年，同样的功能经常被用于：\\n上述段落英文原文为：In 2024, many teams treated \"free model\" as a toy or demo lane. In 2025 and 2026, the same lane is often used for:\\n– 预算批准前的早期功能验证\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Early feature validation before budget approval\\n– 提示词和工具调用原型开发\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Prompt and tool-calling prototyping\\n– 教学、内部培训和黑客松项目\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Classroom, internal training, and hackathon programs\\n– 临时或优雅降级实验\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Overflow or graceful-degradation experiments\\n这会产生新的风险：团队悄悄地让免费功能成为核心基础设施，却未在文档中记录服务预期。\\n上述段落英文原文为：That creates a new risk: teams quietly let free lanes become core infrastructure without writing down service expectations.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">团队容易混淆的地方</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Where teams get confused</quark-heading>\\n他们混淆了三个概念：\\n上述段落英文原文为：They mix up three ideas:\\n– 价格：模型页面显示的每token $0\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Price: $0 per token on the model page\\n– 可靠性：在你的流量模式下调用是否能持续成功\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Reliability: whether calls succeed consistently at your traffic pattern\\n– 一致性：你是否能获得相似的风格、延迟和工具行为\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Consistency: whether you get similar style, latency, and tool behavior over time\\n一个质量优秀的免费模型可能仍然是一个糟糕的生产环境依赖项，如果你的业务需要可预测的行为。\\n上述段落英文原文为：A free model can be excellent in quality and still be a poor production dependency if your business needs predictable behavior.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">现在谁应该关心</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Who should care now</quark-heading>\\n批准发布标准的工程经理\\n上述段落英文原文为：Engineering managers approving launch criteria\\n在面向用户的功能中承诺响应质量的产品经理\\n上述段落英文原文为：PMs promising response quality in user-facing features\\n依赖可重复输出来构建流水线的数据团队\\n上述段落英文原文为：Data teams relying on repeatable outputs for pipelines\\n现代问题不再是\"它是免费的吗？\"而是\"当这个免费路由发生变化时，什么会崩溃？\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：The modern question is not \"Is it free?\" It is \"What breaks when this free route changes?\"\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">免费模型在真实技术栈中的位置</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Where Free Models Fit in a Real Stack</quark-heading>\\n免费模型最好用作你架构中的一个层，而不是整个架构。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Free models are best used as a layer in your architecture, not the whole architecture.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">实用的栈模式</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">A practical stack pattern</quark-heading>\\n使用三条车道：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Use three lanes:\\n– 车道A：用于实验、质量保证和低风险流量的自由车道\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Lane A: Free lane for experiments, QA, and low-risk traffic\\n– 车道B：用于服务等级协议级别用户体验和关键工作流的付费车道\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Lane B: Paid lane for SLA-like user experiences and key workflows\\n– 车道C：用于服务中断或预算保护机制的备用车道\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Lane C: Fallback lane for outages or budget guardrails\\n业务流程\\n上述段落英文原文为：Business Process\\nOpenRouter围绕路由构建。其提供商路由文档显示了负载均衡等默认配置和可选的备用方案。这意味着您可以有意设计行为，而无需希望默认配置对您的产品总是正确的。\\n上述段落英文原文为：OpenRouter is built around routing. Its provider-routing docs show defaults like load balancing and optional fallbacks. That means you can design behavior intentionally, instead of hoping the default is always right for your product.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">免费车道的良好使用场景</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Good use cases for free lanes</quark-heading>\\n关注方向而非确切措辞的提示迭代\\n上述段落英文原文为：Prompt iteration where you care about direction more than exact wording\\n非关键任务的内部协作者\\n上述段落英文原文为：Internal copilots for non-critical tasks\\n需要审核的批量合成数据草稿\\n上述段落英文原文为：Bulk synthetic data drafts that will be reviewed\\n学生或社区功能，明确预期\"尽力而为\"\\n上述段落英文原文为：Student or community features with explicit \"best effort\" expectations\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">仅免费车道的不良使用场景</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Bad use cases for free-only dependence</quark-heading>\\n合同约定的响应时间承诺\\n上述段落英文原文为：Contracted response-time promises\\n保留规则严格但未应用路由策略控制的合规性工作流\\n上述段落英文原文为：Compliance-heavy workflows with strict retention rules but no routing policy controls applied\\n关键任务自动化，单个失败请求就会造成运营损害\\n上述段落英文原文为：Mission-critical automations where one failed request causes operational damage\\n需要在长窗口内稳定、可重现模型行为的评估流水线\\n上述段落英文原文为：Evaluation pipelines that require stable, repeatable model behavior over long windows\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">隐藏的耦合问题</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">The hidden coupling problem</quark-heading>\\n如果您的应用程序逻辑假设使用某种模型人格，但您的路由可以切换模型，那么您的产品语义就会出现漂移：\\n上述段落英文原文为：If your app logic assumes one model personality, but your route can switch models, your product semantics drift:\\n– 不同的拒绝行为\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Different refusal behavior\\n– 不同的工具调用怪癖\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Different tool-calling quirks\\n– 不同的JSON格式严格性\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Different JSON formatting strictness\\n– 不同的延迟和超时配置文件\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Different latency and timeout profile\\n用户称这种情况为\"随机质量日\"，工程师称之为未跟踪的依赖性方差。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Users call this \"random quality days.\" Engineers call it untracked dependency variance.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">谁应该关心</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Who should care</quark-heading>\\n使用单个API密钥构建且可观测性有限的全栈开发者\\n上述段落英文原文为：Full-stack developers building with one API key and little observability\\n在大规模运行入职助手的增长团队\\n上述段落英文原文为：Growth teams running onboarding assistants at scale\\n因意外模型方差而继承故障的客服团队\\n上述段落英文原文为：Support teams that inherit incidents caused by unplanned model variance\\n免费模式最适合作为可控的中间层，具有明确的调用范围，而不是成为所有情况的默认选项。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Free fits best as a controlled layer with clear blast radius, not as an invisible default for everything.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">在依赖之前先评估框架</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Evaluation Framework Before You Depend on It</quark-heading>\\n在团队开始依赖任何OpenRouter免费路由之前，请务必进行一次简短但严格的评估，这个过程可以在几天内完成，无需花费数月时间。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Before your team depends on any OpenRouter free route, run a short but strict evaluation. You can do this in days, not months.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">1. 明确确切的依赖关系</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">1. Clarify the exact dependency</quark-heading>\\n需要明确候选方案是：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Define whether your candidate is:\\n–\\n上述段落英文原文为：–\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n（随机兼容的免费模型）\\n上述段落英文原文为：(random compatible free model)\\n– 具体\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Specific\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nmodel_id:free\\n上述段落英文原文为：model_id:free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n变体\\n上述段落英文原文为：variant\\n这一行配置会改变您的风险评估结果。\\n上述段落英文原文为：This one line changes your risk profile.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">2. 使用日期验证当前限制</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">2. Validate current limits with dates</quark-heading>\\n根据OpenRouter 2026年3月30日的定价说明，免费计划的限制为每天50次请求、每分钟20次请求，同时注明失败尝试仍然计入每日配额。该说明还指出免费计划可访问25多个免费模型和4个免费提供商。拥有至少10美元信用额度的团队可以获得更高的免费模型请求限制（文档中记录的免费模型每日限制为1000次）。\\n上述段落英文原文为：As of March 30, 2026, OpenRouter pricing states free plan limits at 50 requests/day and 20 requests/minute, with notes that failed attempts still count toward daily quota. It also states free-plan access to 25+ free models and 4 free providers. Teams with at least $10 credits can have higher free-model request limits (documented as 1000/day for free models).\\n请勿将这些数值视为永恒不变。务必在架构文档中记录检索日期。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Do not treat these values as timeless. Store the retrieval date in your architecture doc.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">3. 测试行为差异性，而不仅仅是平均质量</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">3. Test for behavior variance, not just average quality</quark-heading>\\n在多天多时间点运行固定提示套件：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Run a fixed prompt suite across multiple days and times:\\n– 功能性提示\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Functional prompts\\n– 工具调用提示\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Tool-calling prompts\\n– 结构化输出提示\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Structured output prompts\\n– 对抗性格式提示\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Adversarial formatting prompts\\n评估通过率和漂移情况。一个一次表现优秀但随时间不一致的模型，不适合严格任务的生产环境。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Score pass rate and drift. A model that is great once but inconsistent over time is not production-ready for strict tasks.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">4. 在您自己的流量模式下测量可靠性</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">4. Measure reliability under your own traffic shape</quark-heading>\\n使用突发流量和稳态测试：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Use burst and steady-state tests:\\n– 低速率下支持1个用户\\n上述段落英文原文为：– 1 user at low rate\\n– 支持20个并发调用\\n上述段落英文原文为：– 20 concurrent calls\\n– 模拟峰值分钟负载\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Peak minute simulation\\n跟踪429错误频率、超时率、中位延迟和p95延迟。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Track 429 frequency, timeout rate, median latency, and p95 latency.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">5. 确定推广标准</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">5. Decide on promotion criteria</quark-heading>\\n在以下任一条件满足时，从免费版推广到付费版：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Promote from free to paid when one of these is true:\\n– 用户界面错误超出容忍范围\\n上述段落英文原文为：– User-facing errors exceed your tolerance\\n– 输出漂移损害用户体验或影响下游解析\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Output drift harms UX or downstream parsing\\n– 请求量接近免费配额上限\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Request volume approaches free quota ceilings\\n– 需要满足合同约定的可靠性要求\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You need contractual reliability expectations\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">6. 立即制定退出计划</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">6. Write the exit plan now</quark-heading>\\n针对每个免费依赖项，明确：\\n上述段落英文原文为：For every free dependency, define:\\n– 付费替代方案模式\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Paid replacement model\\n– 切换触发阈值\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Trigger threshold to switch\\n– 回滚命令或配置标志\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Rollback command or config flag\\n谁应该关注：所有可能意外在免费实验路由上构建生产环境保证的团队。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Who should care: every team that might accidentally build production guarantees on top of a free experimental route.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">风险控制团队跳过的内容</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Risk Controls Teams Skip</quark-heading>\\n大多数免费模型依赖的问题并非模型质量问题，而是控制平面问题。通过简单的控制措施就能大幅降低风险。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Most problems with free model dependence are not model quality problems. They are control-plane problems. You can reduce risk a lot with simple controls.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">控制1：提供商策略过滤器针对敏感数据</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Control 1: Provider policy filters for sensitive data</quark-heading>\\nOpenRouter提供商路由功能包含请求级控制，如\\n上述段落英文原文为：OpenRouter provider-routing features include request-level controls like\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\ndata_collection\\n上述段落英文原文为：data_collection\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n和\\n上述段落英文原文为：and\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nzdr\\n上述段落英文原文为：zdr\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n（零数据保留强制执行）。如果处理敏感输入，这些设置比基准分数更重要。\\n上述段落英文原文为：(zero data retention enforcement). If you process sensitive inputs, these settings matter more than benchmark scores.\\n如果没有策略过滤器，你的\"免费\"选择可能会与内部隐私要求产生冲突。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Without policy filters, your \"free\" choice can conflict with internal privacy requirements.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">控制 2：降级策略</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Control 2: Fallback discipline</quark-heading>\\n降级策略可以提高成功率，但如果你不记录每个请求是由哪个提供商/模型处理的，可能会产生意外行为。请始终持久化响应元数据，包括返回的模型 ID。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Fallbacks increase success rates, but they can also create surprise behavior if you do not log which provider/model served each request. Always persist response metadata, including returned model ID.\\n如果你为了确定性行为而禁用降级策略，需要理解你可能会用一致性来换取可靠性。\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you disable fallbacks for deterministic behavior, understand you may trade reliability for consistency.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">控制 3：模式和工具验证护栏</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Control 3: Schema and tool validation guardrails</quark-heading>\\n如果你依赖结构化输出或工具，请在下游执行前验证每个响应。\\n上述段落英文原文为：If you rely on structured outputs or tools, validate every response before downstream execution.\\n- 拒绝格式错误的 JSON\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Reject malformed JSON\\n- 要求预期的键\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Require expected keys\\n- 验证工具名称和参数模式\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Validate tool name and argument schema\\n当免费路由可能产生不同的模型后端时，这至关重要。\\n上述段落英文原文为：This is essential when free routing can produce different model backends.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">控制 4：环境隔离</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Control 4: Environment separation</quark-heading>\\nOpenRouter 价格 FAQ 明确指出 API 密钥按环境分开管理，并带有配额和警报。请使用这种方法。\\n上述段落英文原文为：OpenRouter pricing FAQ notes separate API keys with caps and alerts per environment. Use that.\\n- 开发密钥：免费重载使用\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Dev key: free heavy usage\\n- 预发布密钥：混合模式\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Staging key: mixed\\n- 生产密钥：付费为主，免费可选降级\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Prod key: paid primary, free optional fallback only\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">控制 5：面向用户的透明度</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Control 5: User-facing transparency</quark-heading>\\n如果某个功能运行在尽力而为的免费通道上，请在产品说明或状态文档中明确说明。清晰的预期比沉默的不一致更有价值。\\n上述段落英文原文为：If a feature runs on a best-effort free lane, say so in product copy or status docs. Clear expectation beats silent inconsistency.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">谁应该关心</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Who should care</quark-heading>\\n安全和合规负责人\\n上述段落英文原文为：Security and compliance owners\\nSRE 和平台工程师\\n上述段落英文原文为：SRE and platform engineers\\n负责用户信任的项目经理\\n上述段落英文原文为：PMs responsible for user trust\\n风险控制不是官僚主义。它们是你保持免费实验优势的方式，同时避免继承随机中断和治理债务。\\n上述段落英文原文为：Risk controls are not bureaucracy. They are how you keep a free experimentation advantage without inheriting random outages and governance debt.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">决策矩阵和30天发布计划</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"2\">Decision Matrix and 30-Day Rollout Plan</quark-heading>\\n如果你的团队现在理解了这些概念，下一步就是制定决策和发布路径。\\n上述段落英文原文为：If your team understands the term now, the next step is a decision and rollout path.\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">快速决策矩阵</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Quick decision matrix</quark-heading>\\n使用\\n上述段落英文原文为：Use\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n适用场景：\\n上述段落英文原文为：when:\\n– 学习、原型开发或演示运行\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You are learning, prototyping, or running demos\\n– 输出结果的差异可以接受\\n上述段落英文原文为：– Output variance is acceptable\\n– 希望零成本探索和快速部署\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You want zero-cost exploration and fast setup\\n使用特定\\n上述段落英文原文为：Use specific\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n:free\\n上述段落英文原文为：:free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n模型的场景：\\n上述段落英文原文为：models when:\\n– 评估期间需要更高的行为可预测性\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You need more behavior predictability during evaluation\\n– 正在深入测试某个模型系列\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You are testing one model family deeply\\n– 可以容忍免费版的使用限制\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You can tolerate free-tier availability limits\\n使用付费模型的场景：\\n上述段落英文原文为：Use paid models when:\\n– 用户承诺与速度或一致性相关\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You have user promises tied to speed or consistency\\n– 需要的吞吐量超过免费配额\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You need higher throughput than free quotas\\n– 核心工作流需要更强的运营信心保障\\n上述段落英文原文为：– You need stronger operational confidence for core workflows\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">30天实际部署</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">30-day practical rollout</quark-heading>\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">第1周：基准测试和监控指标设置</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Week 1: Baseline and instrumentation</quark-heading>\\n选择一条\\n上述段落英文原文为：Choose one\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nopenrouter/free\\n上述段落英文原文为：openrouter/free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n路径和一个特定的\\n上述段落英文原文为：path and one specific\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\n:free\\n上述段落英文原文为：:free\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n候选模型\\n上述段落英文原文为：candidate\\n添加日志记录，用于记录使用的模型、延迟、错误和配额失败情况\\n上述段落英文原文为：Add logging for model used, latency, errors, and quota failures\\n创建包含30-50个提示的评估数据集\\n上述段落英文原文为：Create a 30-50 prompt evaluation set\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">第2周：可靠性测试和漂移测试</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Week 2: Reliability and drift testing</quark-heading>\\n运行每日计划评估\\n上述段落英文原文为：Run daily scheduled evaluations\\n模拟真实峰值负载\\n上述段落英文原文为：Simulate realistic peak load\\n比较各路由的通过率差异\\n上述段落英文原文为：Compare pass rate variance across routes\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">第3周：治理和路由策略</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Week 3: Governance and routing policy</quark-heading>\\n应用\\n上述段落英文原文为：Apply\\n<quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-code>\\nzdr\\n上述段落英文原文为：zdr\\n</quark-code>\\n上述段落英文原文为：</quark-code>\\n或数据收集约束条件\\n上述段落英文原文为：or data-collection constraints where needed\\n明确定义降级行为\\n上述段落英文原文为：Define fallback behavior explicitly\\n分离环境的API密钥和配额限制\\n上述段落英文原文为：Separate environment API keys and caps\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">第4周：生产决策</quark-heading>\\n上述段落英文原文为：<quark-heading level=\"3\">Week 4: Production decision</quark-heading>\\n决定采用免费模式、混合模式还是付费优先模式\\n上述段落英文原文为：Decide free-only, mixed, or paid-primary architecture\\n记录自动触发付费推广的阈值\\n上述段落英文原文为：Document thresholds that auto-trigger paid promotion\\n向支持和产